1
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:43,020
Something will work out.

2
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:59,880
Anyone without a job, come to me.

3
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:04,480
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

4
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:18,220
Look, even Akane-mu's burning out;
it'll all work out eventually.

5
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:27,540
You understand, right? Got it, got it.
Once you do, gather round and follow me.

6
00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:43,380
Ryo-san declares his passionate love!

7
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:51,820
Wow, you've even detailed
every single screw!

8
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:57,000
My remote-control building is all about pursuing realism to the extreme,
you know.

9
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,820
Chief, good morning!

10
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:00,100
Good morning.

11
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:01,100
Good morning.

12
00:02:01,100 --> 00:02:03,720
Ryo-chan.

13
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,450
Ah

14
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:11,280
Chief! Don't suddenly shout like that!
Look what you've done to the tank!

15
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:13,720
I've been building it
all night since yesterday!

16
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:18,260
Idiot! It's your fault for building
that kind of thing during work hours!

17
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:19,760
Never mind that, look at this!

18
00:02:20,820 --> 00:02:22,320
W-what's this?

19
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:24,080
It's an omiai photo.

20
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:27,440
I'm not the least bit
interested in marriage.

21
00:02:27,860 --> 00:02:32,080
Shut up!
A slob like you should get himself a wife!

22
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:33,840
Mind your own business.

23
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:44,500
I gathered these from everyone at the office and the neighborhood. Just look at them, at least.
Ugh, you're so persistent. Have you forgotten about Sato Miyai, the one you recommended to me a few years ago, Chief?

24
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:52,360
Dragged here without even showing me the photo...
Is that Mr. Ohara?

25
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:56,260
Ando has been waiting for you too.

26
00:02:56,860 --> 00:03:00,400
Sorry we're late. Hey, let's go.

27
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:06,260
Nice to meet you.
This is Senior Officer Kankichi Ryotsu.

28
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:10,680
Dah, well then,
allow me to introduce us as well.

29
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:18,420
This is my mother, Yasuyo Takahashi. Pleased to meet you.
I'm her daughter, Yoshie, and this is my son's child, Iuka.

30
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:19,420
Hello.

31
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:20,560
Hello.

32
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:22,920
What a cute little girl.

33
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:25,220
Chief, you brought the little one along,
didn't you?

34
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:26,700
Don't be so picky.

35
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:29,720
Shouldn't you just be grateful
she's willing to meet you?

36
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:32,900
Besides, she's quite a lovely young lady,
isn't she?

37
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:36,960
No way, that's a lie.

38
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:40,180
Seems like you're not entirely opposed to it

39
00:03:40,780 --> 00:03:42,760
Well then, we'll be taking our leave now.

40
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:44,920
Now it's up to the two of you.

41
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:45,920
Yes, that's right.

42
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:48,520
Yes, well then, Mom, you take care now.

43
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:49,320
Yes.

44
00:03:49,860 --> 00:03:51,220
Yuu, let's go.

45
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:51,820
Okay.

46
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:55,260
Isn't the person for that
arranged meeting you...

47
00:03:55,260 --> 00:03:58,460
Oh my, I already have a husband.

48
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:01,500
Then who is the matchmaking partner?

49
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:07,760
Jojo Butcher

50
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:12,120
It's no laughing matter!

51
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:15,600
Try putting yourself in my shoes, being made to go
on a blind date without even checking who I'm meeting.

52
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:19,120
Sorry, but that really is the Chief's fault.

53
00:04:19,740 --> 00:04:22,020
I really am sorry about that.

54
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:25,840
I heard she'd lost her
husband and had one daughter,

55
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:29,620
so I went and assumed
it was the younger girl.

56
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:33,900
My poor, pure little heart
was torn to shreds, you know.

57
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:36,480
I never want to go through that again.

58
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,760
I'll return this to you.

59
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:43,100
After that omiai,
you cursed at me endlessly,

60
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:46,740
and then made me treat you to 30,000 yen worth of sushi.
I remember that now.

61
00:04:46,740 --> 00:04:47,400
Gulp!

62
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:50,400
Yes, there was that too, wasn't there.

63
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:51,500
Shut up!

64
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:54,700
Anyway,
pick one from these and go to the omiai.

65
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:56,200
That's an order.

66
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:57,240
Understood?

67
00:04:58,500 --> 00:04:59,220
Chief...

68
00:04:59,220 --> 00:05:01,100
Seriously, I'm not joking around!

69
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:02,400
Who'd want an omiai?

70
00:05:04,180 --> 00:05:05,380
Ryo-chan...

71
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:09,280
The Chief is worried about you,
Ryo-chan, which is why he's pushing this.

72
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:12,520
What's wrong?

73
00:05:13,100 --> 00:05:13,760
Look at this!

74
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:14,960
Oh my.

75
00:05:15,540 --> 00:05:16,720
She's really beautiful, isn't she?

76
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:18,480
Ryo-san, come take a look!

77
00:05:21,840 --> 00:05:25,720
I never expected the Chief
to bring me such a beauty.

78
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:28,400
Ryo-san,
you absolutely should go to this meeting.

79
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:29,980
R-really?

80
00:05:32,060 --> 00:05:34,440
Ryotsu has agreed to the meeting!

81
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:36,780
That's good to hear.

82
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:37,780
Well, the thing is...

83
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:39,900
Is something wrong?

84
00:05:40,460 --> 00:05:42,300
It's this young lady, though.

85
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:45,600
I thought so.

86
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:47,220
What do you mean, you thought so?

87
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:52,180
Since it's Ryotsu, I figured he'd
pick Miss Yoshinaga's daughter.

88
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:54,680
So you know her?

89
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:58,280
Yes, we often see each other
at the flower arranging club.

90
00:05:58,280 --> 00:06:01,440
She's very humble and polite,
a lovely young lady.

91
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:05,780
She does seem that way,
but isn't she too good for Ryotsu?

92
00:06:05,780 --> 00:06:09,500
Is that so? I think they're a good match.

93
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:15,160
Getting Ryo-san settled down has been your lifelong dream,
hasn't it?

94
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:17,560
Let's definitely get them together.

95
00:06:19,740 --> 00:06:21,140
But that's probably impossible.

96
00:06:25,280 --> 00:06:27,940
This is Police Sergeant Kankichi Ryotsu.

97
00:06:27,940 --> 00:06:29,460
Nice to meet you.

98
00:06:29,460 --> 00:06:31,560
This is Makoto-san.

99
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:33,940
I'm Makoto Yoshinaga.

100
00:06:33,940 --> 00:06:37,300
I may not be much,
but I look forward to your kindness.

101
00:06:39,040 --> 00:06:40,360
Likewise.

102
00:06:40,820 --> 00:06:43,380
Makoto-san, let's skip the stiff greetings.

103
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:45,400
Let's keep things casual today.

104
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:46,800
Yes, ma'am.

105
00:06:47,260 --> 00:06:49,040
You look so good in a kimono, too.

106
00:06:54,140 --> 00:06:56,440
Wait, don't tell me that
old lady over there is...

107
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:58,720
...the one I'm meeting, right?

108
00:06:58,720 --> 00:07:01,640
Ryotsu: Of course not!

109
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:06,280
But the Chief does have a track
record of mixing up matches.

110
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:12,980
Baya, our live-in nanny, has been helping
around the house since I was a baby.

111
00:07:12,980 --> 00:07:14,380
Thank you very much.

112
00:07:15,380 --> 00:07:16,220
Ryotsu-san.

113
00:07:16,220 --> 00:07:20,880
Police officers who protect the peace
of the town and our safe everyday lives

114
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:22,680
are such admirable jobs.

115
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:31,760
M-Makoto-san.

116
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:32,380
Yes?

117
00:07:32,380 --> 00:07:33,420
What are your hobbies?

118
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:34,820
I enjoy listening to music.

119
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:37,040
Classical music, I presume?

120
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:39,560
Yes, I love Mozart.

121
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:42,880
Mozart?

122
00:07:43,260 --> 00:07:45,100
Do you listen to it too, Ryo-san?

123
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:49,540
No... I like the katsu sandwiches
at the Mozart coffee shop, though.

124
00:07:49,980 --> 00:07:50,300
Well...

125
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:53,000
Hello.

126
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,300
Ryo-san, what are your hobbies?

127
00:07:55,300 --> 00:07:58,560
Ah, horses, a little.

128
00:07:58,560 --> 00:08:03,200
Horses? I love horses too.
I often go riding.

129
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:05,900
Do you ride British style, or Western?

130
00:08:07,300 --> 00:08:12,140
I've been to a few places,
but usually I'm not allowed to ride there.

131
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:15,380
You don't mean horse racing, do you?

132
00:08:16,020 --> 00:08:17,620
Oh no, I messed up!

133
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:22,740
Ryo-san,
you really have a great sense of humor.

134
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:24,580
Hello.

135
00:08:26,020 --> 00:08:28,000
You seem to be having so much fun.

136
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:33,700
Alright, come on, come here, over here!

137
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:36,200
Wow, they've all gathered like this!

138
00:08:37,300 --> 00:08:37,580
Amazing!

139
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:38,227
Well,

140
00:08:38,277 --> 00:08:42,100
It's because I'm always made to feed the
fish in the pond at my relative's sushi shop.

141
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:46,980
Unfortunately,
I don't have any food with me.

142
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:54,140
Hey! Makoto-san's kimono
is going to get wet!

143
00:08:54,380 --> 00:08:54,760
Wait!

144
00:08:57,140 --> 00:08:58,240
Ryo-san!

145
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,280
That idiot!

146
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:03,900
Oh my, how terrible. What a fun person.

147
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:10,040
Ryo-san, are you all right?

148
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:12,000
Well...

149
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,720
Your kimono will get wet, so...

150
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,320
I don't care about the kimono!

151
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:16,720
Come on, hurry!

152
00:09:17,660 --> 00:09:18,940
Sorry.

153
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:30,640
Well, this is hopeless.

154
00:09:40,420 --> 00:09:42,380
Senpai, how did it go?

155
00:09:42,950 --> 00:09:44,820
The matchmaking, of course.

156
00:09:46,280 --> 00:09:48,100
She was a nice girl, though.

157
00:09:48,820 --> 00:09:50,300
It's Kankichi Ryotsu.

158
00:09:50,940 --> 00:09:53,260
I heard you had a
matchmaking meeting yesterday.

159
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:54,580
Yeah, well.

160
00:09:54,580 --> 00:09:57,600
Judging by that face,
it sounds like a total disaster.

161
00:09:57,600 --> 00:10:01,940
No woman in this world would ever take
a liking to a gorilla-faced man, right?

162
00:10:01,940 --> 00:10:03,640
Shut up, leave me alone.

163
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:04,580
Ryotsu!

164
00:10:04,580 --> 00:10:06,720
This is bad!

165
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:11,220
What is it, Chief? Why are you in such a hurry?
Did you hit a jackpot at the races?

166
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:13,660
Something even bigger has happened.

167
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:16,480
Don't tell me, a hundred-thousand-yen ticket,
or no, a million-yen one?

168
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:19,320
Idiot, it's not that.
I can hardly believe it, but -

169
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:24,480
Makoto-san has contacted us saying she
likes you and wants to start dating you.

170
00:10:27,180 --> 00:10:28,857
This must be a dream. Honda,

171
00:10:28,907 --> 00:10:31,420
pinch my cheek as hard as you can.

172
00:10:34,780 --> 00:10:36,600
Hey, what are you doing?

173
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:39,140
That's cruel, senpai!

174
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:41,460
You're the one who told me to pinch you!

175
00:10:43,280 --> 00:10:44,980
Then could it be...?

176
00:10:44,980 --> 00:10:46,050
It's not a dream,

177
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:50,260
Makoto really seems to
have taken a liking to you.

178
00:10:50,260 --> 00:10:51,500
No way!

179
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:52,600
Haa...

180
00:10:53,300 --> 00:10:54,300
Yes!

181
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:10,200
So women who appreciate my good qualities really do exist,
after all.

182
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:12,840
Liking Ryotsu Kankichi, of all people?

183
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:15,860
She'd have to be a real oddball or a volunteer,
for sure.

184
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:19,300
Or maybe a gorilla woman even
uglier than Ryotsu Kankichi.

185
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:20,320
That's right!

186
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:23,220
Go ahead and badmouth me, I don't mind,

187
00:11:24,300 --> 00:11:25,240
but don't say nasty things!

188
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:28,000
Hey, cut it out!

189
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,660
Violence isn't allowed, you know.

190
00:11:29,660 --> 00:11:31,300
Let me go, Chief!

191
00:11:31,540 --> 00:11:32,820
Just calm down already.

192
00:11:32,820 --> 00:11:35,680
Makoto-san, compared to you lot,

193
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:38,220
is like the moon and a turtle,
no, like Bob Sapp

194
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:40,080
and a toilet mop.
That's how big the difference is!

195
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:41,960
A toilet?

196
00:11:42,260 --> 00:11:42,980
A mop?

197
00:11:43,540 --> 00:11:44,680
I said "now" too, didn't I!

198
00:11:44,900 --> 00:11:48,400
You, the number one man who hasn't wanted
to get married for twenty years straight,

199
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:49,900
don't get to say that to me!

200
00:11:50,260 --> 00:11:51,780
What did you say? Makoto-san is...

201
00:11:51,780 --> 00:11:56,880
the very picture of a Yamato nadeshiko,
so gentle, graceful, and wonderful!

202
00:11:56,880 --> 00:11:58,600
H-hey, stop that!

203
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:01,280
Excuse me for interrupting
while you're busy.

204
00:12:04,280 --> 00:12:05,480
Makoto-san.

205
00:12:06,180 --> 00:12:06,640
Hello.

206
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:07,720
Hello.

207
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:10,100
Surprised?

208
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:11,120
N-no way.

209
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:13,920
T-this has to be a nightmare!

210
00:12:16,210 --> 00:12:18,380
Why isn't this a dream?

211
00:12:18,860 --> 00:12:22,020
That's why I said you two
are a pair of sap and mop.

212
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:25,200
Toishin is no different from us either.

213
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:27,100
And her figure is way too good.

214
00:12:27,100 --> 00:12:29,360
Hey, don't stare.

215
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:30,500
That's rude.

216
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:32,820
Makoto-san, what brings you here today?

217
00:12:33,680 --> 00:12:36,120
I know it's a bit presumptuous, but

218
00:12:36,780 --> 00:12:39,240
I brought a lunch for Ryotsu-san.

219
00:12:39,240 --> 00:12:40,240
Really?

220
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:43,700
Would you mind eating it?

221
00:12:44,860 --> 00:12:46,160
Ryo-chan is overwhelmed!

222
00:12:46,160 --> 00:12:47,780
I'll eat, I'll eat!

223
00:12:48,380 --> 00:12:50,920
Wow, that bento looks delicious!

224
00:12:51,540 --> 00:12:53,060
Hey, senpai.

225
00:12:53,060 --> 00:12:54,240
Y-yeah.

226
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:56,800
Well then, please, go ahead and eat.

227
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:58,120
Y-yes.

228
00:13:00,980 --> 00:13:02,540
Well then, I'll dig in.

229
00:13:02,540 --> 00:13:05,720
Delicious!

230
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:10,200
The salt on this ayu is perfect too,
Makoto-san.

231
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:13,060
I'm glad you enjoyed it.

232
00:13:13,060 --> 00:13:16,000
Chief and Honda, you should try some too!

233
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,760
Thank you for the food.

234
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:23,240
Delicious.

235
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:26,020
It really looks like food
from a high-class restaurant.

236
00:13:26,020 --> 00:13:29,320
You never cook, you just eat
convenience store bento all the time.

237
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:31,640
Unlike some women I could name

238
00:13:31,640 --> 00:13:32,900
What's that supposed to mean?

239
00:13:33,420 --> 00:13:35,540
Maybe it really is restaurant food.

240
00:13:35,540 --> 00:13:38,600
Or maybe she just transferred
it into a jūbako box.

241
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:40,860
That is absolutely not the case.

242
00:13:40,860 --> 00:13:45,580
My young lady has been working since
early morning for Ryotsu-sama's sake,

243
00:13:45,580 --> 00:13:48,080
and she made it all by herself,
with heartfelt care.

244
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:51,140
This old nanny swears
before heaven and earth,

245
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:52,760
that there is no such thing.

246
00:13:53,380 --> 00:13:53,740
Yes.

247
00:13:54,400 --> 00:13:55,360
Ryo-sama.

248
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:00,160
Maria

249
00:14:00,160 --> 00:14:01,220
Ryo-sama

250
00:14:02,020 --> 00:14:03,780
Reiko told me all about it.

251
00:14:03,780 --> 00:14:05,540
Even though you have someone like me?

252
00:14:05,540 --> 00:14:07,920
I can't forgive you for
going on a matchmaking meeting.

253
00:14:09,340 --> 00:14:12,540
Please calm down.

254
00:14:13,340 --> 00:14:15,460
Ryotsu-san, are you all right?

255
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:17,320
I'm fine.

256
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:18,400
Who is she?

257
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:21,600
This woman,
being so familiar with my Ryo-sama?

258
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:24,460
Maria-chan,
she's Kankichi Ryotsu's matchmaking partner.

259
00:14:24,460 --> 00:14:25,720
What did you say?

260
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:27,720
Hey, you!

261
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:32,660
Ryo-sama and I spent the night together in Ryo-sama's room.
We're that close.

262
00:14:32,660 --> 00:14:35,180
So there was such a woman?

263
00:14:35,180 --> 00:14:36,640
Makoto-san, it's a misunderstanding!

264
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:37,580
Maria is...

265
00:14:39,340 --> 00:14:40,660
I see. So that's how it is.

266
00:14:43,100 --> 00:14:44,440
I won't allow it.

267
00:14:44,440 --> 00:14:46,840
Maria-chan

268
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:57,780
No way.

269
00:14:57,780 --> 00:15:00,780
Sorry, but I'm a fifth-dan in aikido.

270
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:05,180
Are you all right? Did you get hurt?

271
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:08,920
I lost.

272
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:12,800
Maria-chan, what happened to being
the epitome of Japanese womanhood?

273
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:15,220
She's way more of a wild mare than we are!

274
00:15:15,220 --> 00:15:18,400
Yes, yes. Forgive me for talking back, but

275
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:21,780
she only took up aikido as a hobby.

276
00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:27,300
Miss Makoto is a licensed master of ikebana,
tea ceremony, Japanese dance, and koto.

277
00:15:28,240 --> 00:15:29,500
R-really?

278
00:15:29,840 --> 00:15:35,040
Yes, even from my perspective as her nanny,
she's a flawless young lady.

279
00:15:35,520 --> 00:15:36,620
Excuse me for a moment.

280
00:15:36,620 --> 00:15:39,560
Yes, let me show you.

281
00:15:58,260 --> 00:15:59,660
Please, do help yourself.

282
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:03,900
I don't know anything about tea ceremony,
so I'll just drink it however I like.

283
00:16:04,360 --> 00:16:06,220
Please don't mind it and drink up.

284
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:13,240
I expected it to be more bitter,
but it's surprisingly good.

285
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:14,860
Reiko, want to try some?

286
00:16:14,860 --> 00:16:16,020
Y-yes.

287
00:16:30,680 --> 00:16:31,640
I'll gratefully accept it.

288
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:48,120
It's excellent, thank you for the tea.

289
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:49,740
Could I have a plate?

290
00:16:50,740 --> 00:16:52,160
Komachi, Naoko.

291
00:16:52,160 --> 00:16:55,320
Are you still going to
badmouth Makoto after all this?

292
00:16:58,880 --> 00:17:01,460
Looks like you've realized your mistake

293
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:04,540
Reiko, listen to me!

294
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:06,960
What's wrong, you two?

295
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:09,980
Earlier, while I was doing traffic
enforcement during the commute...

296
00:17:13,080 --> 00:17:13,880
Naoko

297
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:17,380
Kankichi Ryotsu

298
00:17:17,380 --> 00:17:18,820
Good work.

299
00:17:19,520 --> 00:17:21,040
I apologize for the other day.

300
00:17:21,500 --> 00:17:22,400
No, the apologies are mine.

301
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:22,840
Thanks.

302
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:28,380
Get to work protecting the peace of the
town and the safety of the citizens' lives.

303
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:30,540
Well then, let's go, Makoto-san.

304
00:17:30,540 --> 00:17:32,000
Yes, Ryo-chan.

305
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:36,620
So, you know, the Chief is like,

306
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:39,320
"Ever since Ryo-san..."

307
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:48,160
they're practically flaunting it,
acting like a couple already.

308
00:17:49,040 --> 00:17:50,120
I can't forgive this.

309
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:52,280
Why does a gorilla-faced guy
like that get all the attention?

310
00:17:56,680 --> 00:18:01,740
Reiko-san! Reiko-san, what's wrong? Ah...

311
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:08,540
Someone finally came along who appreciates Ryo-chan's good qualities, so we should be happy for him.
Is that right?

312
00:18:15,300 --> 00:18:16,480
Aaaaaah!

313
00:18:21,260 --> 00:18:22,420
What a speed!

314
00:18:22,420 --> 00:18:24,380
We've modified it quite a bit.

315
00:18:24,380 --> 00:18:27,440
We can't play without a place this wide.

316
00:18:27,860 --> 00:18:28,620
Hey, hey!

317
00:18:28,620 --> 00:18:31,600
Showing off in broad daylight

318
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:35,160
Think you could lend me some pocket money?

319
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:37,780
Brats are in the way, Chiruchiru.

320
00:18:37,780 --> 00:18:38,980
Ryo-san

321
00:18:38,980 --> 00:18:41,360
Makoto-san, there's no need to worry.

322
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:43,600
Don't you try to look cool!

323
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:45,100
Come on, hand over the money quietly.

324
00:18:46,480 --> 00:18:48,300
You're not talking to me, are you?

325
00:18:48,300 --> 00:18:49,260
What did you say?

326
00:18:49,260 --> 00:18:51,080
Do you want to get hurt?

327
00:18:52,980 --> 00:18:54,400
Mister Ryotsu!

328
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:55,700
Our apologies.

329
00:18:55,700 --> 00:18:59,980
To drive off such scary
people with just one word...

330
00:19:00,900 --> 00:19:03,740
I like you even more now, Mr. Ryotsu.

331
00:19:08,980 --> 00:19:10,780
This can't possibly go this smoothly.

332
00:19:10,780 --> 00:19:12,300
It's going too smoothly.

333
00:19:22,540 --> 00:19:23,560
Makoto-san

334
00:19:23,560 --> 00:19:26,720
Someone like Makoto-san

335
00:19:26,720 --> 00:19:28,700
a flawless young lady

336
00:19:28,700 --> 00:19:30,420
why would she agree to a marriage
meeting with a man like me?

337
00:19:30,420 --> 00:19:31,840
Why would she agree to a marriage
meeting with a man like me?

338
00:19:31,840 --> 00:19:34,440
The men around her surely
wouldn't leave her alone.

339
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:37,260
Shouldn't you be honest with me by now?

340
00:19:37,260 --> 00:19:38,420
Ryo-san,

341
00:19:38,420 --> 00:19:39,740
you're so mature.

342
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:42,200
I'll explain properly.

343
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:50,480
Ever since I was a child,
my dream was to become a fashion designer.

344
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:52,720
What a wonderful dream.

345
00:19:53,220 --> 00:19:56,680
So I was determined to
study abroad in Paris.

346
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:58,320
I told my parents about it, but

347
00:19:59,120 --> 00:20:00,280
they opposed it right away.

348
00:20:01,020 --> 00:20:04,660
They told me to stop chasing such
childish dreams and get married.

349
00:20:04,660 --> 00:20:09,520
So, in desperation,
without even my parents' permission,

350
00:20:09,520 --> 00:20:14,540
I went on a marriage meeting with Ryo-san,
and yes, that's exactly what happened.

351
00:20:15,620 --> 00:20:19,080
But after dating you like this,
Ryo-san, I finally understood.

352
00:20:19,980 --> 00:20:22,100
I... Ryo-san, wait!

353
00:20:23,820 --> 00:20:28,680
Don't say such rash things after
only meeting a few times. Sorry.

354
00:20:31,220 --> 00:20:33,260
I'm done. I'm not going to see you anymore,
starting today.

355
00:20:33,740 --> 00:20:34,440
Ryo-san.

356
00:20:34,440 --> 00:20:37,700
I'm not the type to give up just
because my parents opposed it.

357
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:40,860
I absolutely hate people
who give up on their dreams.

358
00:20:40,860 --> 00:20:42,240
Sorry, but it's over between us.

359
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:43,220
Later.

360
00:20:48,700 --> 00:20:49,620
Ryo-san

361
00:20:50,580 --> 00:20:56,100
Kankichi Ryotsu got dumped?

362
00:20:56,500 --> 00:20:58,360
Sounds like he's been quietly moping.

363
00:20:58,680 --> 00:20:59,620
Hey, Reiko.

364
00:20:59,620 --> 00:21:00,080
Yeah.

365
00:21:00,540 --> 00:21:02,300
I thought something was off.

366
00:21:02,620 --> 00:21:05,940
She finally saw Kankichi Ryotsu's true colors,
that girl.

367
00:21:06,340 --> 00:21:09,620
That gorilla man's act was bound
to fall apart sooner or later

368
00:21:10,020 --> 00:21:11,840
Komachi-chan.

369
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:19,180
What's with you guys?

370
00:21:19,180 --> 00:21:21,760
Looking at me with that tragic
hero face like I'm some pitiful guy.

371
00:21:22,160 --> 00:21:24,920
You were probably saying
"serves him right" after I got dumped, weren't you?

372
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:25,980
Ryo-chan...

373
00:21:25,980 --> 00:21:28,540
Don't you dare feel sorry for me, got it?

374
00:21:28,540 --> 00:21:32,500
I never thought that brat was
anything special to begin with.

375
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:33,440
R-really?

376
00:21:33,840 --> 00:21:34,580
Damn right.

377
00:21:34,580 --> 00:21:38,940
A prissy little miss like
that is totally not my type.

378
00:21:38,940 --> 00:21:43,320
I like stylish women in their thirties
who are at the peak of their charm.

379
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:45,160
Are you forcing yourself?

380
00:21:45,740 --> 00:21:46,960
As if I would.

381
00:21:47,700 --> 00:21:48,780
Anyway, Honda.

382
00:21:49,240 --> 00:21:51,020
You're done with work already, right?

383
00:21:51,020 --> 00:21:51,560
Yeah.

384
00:21:52,140 --> 00:21:54,220
Keep me company tonight.

385
00:21:54,820 --> 00:21:55,540
Understood.

386
00:21:56,160 --> 00:21:57,680
That's the Dutch Corder spirit!

387
00:21:57,680 --> 00:21:59,900
Alright! Let's go out and have a blast!

388
00:22:02,180 --> 00:22:04,200
Don't drink too much.

389
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:05,840
See you.

390
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:20,820
Old man, give me a couple more bottles.

391
00:22:21,280 --> 00:22:24,380
Ryo-san, shouldn't you stop now?

392
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:27,620
Pour me one, or I'll arrest you.

393
00:22:27,620 --> 00:22:29,940
Geez, what can you do?

394
00:22:30,480 --> 00:22:31,820
See, you drank it.

395
00:22:31,820 --> 00:22:34,300
Weren't you going to keep
me company until morning?

396
00:22:34,300 --> 00:22:35,680
Wake up.

397
00:22:36,860 --> 00:22:38,120
I can't drink any more.

398
00:22:38,860 --> 00:22:39,840
Give me a break.

399
00:22:39,840 --> 00:22:41,260
Is that really okay?
Right when it's getting good.

400
00:22:43,700 --> 00:22:45,540
Geez, you're hopeless.

401
00:22:46,340 --> 00:22:47,780
I'll keep you company.

402
00:22:50,660 --> 00:22:51,460
Chief.

403
00:22:52,080 --> 00:22:53,860
Old man, one for me too.

404
00:22:53,860 --> 00:22:54,900
Same again for me.

405
00:22:58,420 --> 00:23:01,420
I'm so glad the Chief is keeping me company!

406
00:23:01,860 --> 00:23:03,440
Keep them coming!

407
00:23:06,100 --> 00:23:08,480
They say the dumber the kid,
the more adorable.

408
00:23:10,480 --> 00:23:11,300
Delicious.

409
00:23:12,240 --> 00:23:14,040
Come on, Ryotsu, drink up!

410
00:23:14,040 --> 00:23:15,280
Thanks.

411
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:21,080
You're a complete idiot.

412
00:23:22,320 --> 00:23:25,060
I heard about it from Makoto's mom.

413
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:27,240
She apparently was grateful.

414
00:23:29,260 --> 00:23:31,360
After you gave her a piece of your mind,

415
00:23:31,360 --> 00:23:32,220
Makoto-san,

416
00:23:32,220 --> 00:23:33,820
after persuading her parents,

417
00:23:33,820 --> 00:23:36,500
she got them to let her study in Paris,
apparently.

418
00:23:37,780 --> 00:23:38,580
Is that so?

419
00:23:38,580 --> 00:23:39,420
Well, that's...

420
00:23:45,980 --> 00:23:46,920
Unlike you,

421
00:23:46,920 --> 00:23:48,220
trying to look cool.

422
00:23:48,220 --> 00:23:49,480
I see.

423
00:23:49,480 --> 00:23:51,040
Good, good.

424
00:23:51,040 --> 00:23:51,740
Chief.

425
00:23:51,740 --> 00:23:52,860
Go ahead, go ahead.

426
00:23:52,860 --> 00:23:54,820
She really liked you, though.

427
00:23:55,980 --> 00:23:58,840
Stop calling me a big fool, you fool!

428
00:24:00,400 --> 00:24:02,100
She was quite a woman, wasn't she?

429
00:24:26,980 --> 00:24:28,260
Maki, chaka-maki, sara-maki

430
00:24:28,260 --> 00:24:30,200
Anything-maki, maki-maki...
what should I do?

431
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:31,640
Right!

432
00:24:32,280 --> 00:24:34,160
Do you have California rolls?

433
00:24:34,160 --> 00:24:36,220
We don't have California rolls.

434
00:24:37,180 --> 00:24:38,940
This isn't America, you know.

435
00:24:39,560 --> 00:24:40,320
I'm sorry.

436
00:24:41,520 --> 00:24:44,380
Uh, excuse me.

437
00:24:45,380 --> 00:24:46,180
Welcome!

438
00:24:47,500 --> 00:24:49,760
Then, kushi-age, kaki-age, katsu-age.

439
00:24:49,760 --> 00:24:51,620
Anything-age-age... what was it again?

440
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:53,580
What do you recommend?

441
00:24:54,600 --> 00:24:56,900
Just watch out for the katsu-age...
I mean, shakedowns.

442
00:24:56,900 --> 00:25:00,580
Was that a dad joke?

443
00:25:00,900 --> 00:25:02,220
Yes, sorry.

444
00:25:02,220 --> 00:25:04,680
I don't get it.

445
00:25:08,060 --> 00:25:09,100
Seriously?

446
00:25:09,300 --> 00:25:10,980
Welcome!

447
00:25:10,980 --> 00:25:13,080
Welcome, come in!

448
00:25:13,920 --> 00:25:15,760
Welcome!

449
00:25:15,760 --> 00:25:17,860
Welcome, come in!

450
00:25:17,860 --> 00:25:20,460
Welcome!

451
00:25:20,460 --> 00:25:22,540
Welcome, come in!

452
00:25:23,620 --> 00:25:27,020
Welcome, welcome!

453
00:25:30,340 --> 00:25:32,540
The scar I found on the
Sumida River embankment

454
00:25:32,540 --> 00:25:33,850
was from when I was in junior high,

455
00:25:33,900 --> 00:25:37,680
when three of us rode one
motorcycle and fell into the river.

456
00:25:38,220 --> 00:25:42,062
Memories of that junior high time,
full of fights and pranks,

457
00:25:42,112 --> 00:25:43,460
are vividly coming back to me now.

458
00:25:43,460 --> 00:25:46,960
Next time, Asakusa Shonen Glen Tine,
see you then!

